WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.427
Task-oriented behavior: get the work done well.

2
00:00:04.477 --> 00:00:12.720
In Yukl’s taxonomy this is category one of four, behaviors one to four of the fifteen the survey measures,

3
00:00:12.770 --> 00:00:18.118
and its objective is to accomplish the work efficiently and reliably.

4
00:00:18.168 --> 00:00:24.768
New managers skip it most, because they assume the team already knows what they know.

5
00:00:24.818 --> 00:00:32.513
The team does not. Behavior one, planning: before the quarter, three priorities, an owner for each,

6
00:00:32.563 --> 00:00:36.816
and a decision about what moves if a new request lands.

7
00:00:36.866 --> 00:00:43.544
Behavior two, clarifying: every person can say, without notes, what they own, by when,

8
00:00:43.594 --> 00:00:49.255
and what done well means; it is written in Culture Amp, not in your head.

9
00:00:49.305 --> 00:00:55.983
Behavior three, monitoring: you look at the work in progress in the weekly one-on-one,

10
00:00:56.033 --> 00:00:59.191
not the finished product on the due date.

11
00:00:59.241 --> 00:01:07.092
Behavior four, problem solving: when something breaks twice, you find the cause and change something,

12
00:01:07.142 --> 00:01:12.490
instead of fixing it a third time yourself. Watch for the difference.

13
00:01:12.540 --> 00:01:20.392
The habit is assuming, emailing the goal once, checking when it is late, and doing the work yourself.

14
00:01:20.442 --> 00:01:26.729
The Vanderbilt way is written, confirmed, checked weekly, and fixed at the cause.

15
00:01:26.779 --> 00:01:32.597
Now flip the four cards below, then turn the page and make your first call.

